{title: Joy to the World}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}

[D]Joy to the world! the [G]Lord [A7]is [D]come;
Let [G]earth re[D]ceive [A7]her [D]King;
Let [D]every [A7]heart pre[D]pare Him [A7]room,
[D]And heaven and nature sing,
[A7]And heaven and nature sing,
And [D]heaven, and [G]heaven and [A7]nature [D]sing.

[D]Joy to the earth! the [G]Sav[A7]ior [D]reigns;
Let [G]men their [D]songs [A7]em[D]ploy;
While [D]fields and [A7]floods, rocks, [D]hills, and [A7]plains
[D]Repeat the sounding joy,
[A7]Repeat the sounding joy,
Re[D]peat, re[G]peat the [A7]sounding [D]joy.

[D]He rules the world with [G]truth [A7]and [D]grace,
And [G]makes the [D]na[A7]tions [D]prove
The [D]glories [A7]of His [D]righteous[A7]ness,
[D]And wonders of His love,
[A7]And wonders of His love,
And [D]wonders, [G]wonders [A7]of His [D]love.
